      "id": 1,
      "text": "New Odanah is located on the Bad River Indian Reservation, the home of the Bad River Band of Lake Superior Chippewa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Odanah%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Wild rice, known as manoomin, and the Kakagon and Bad River sloughs define the cultural identity of New Odanah.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greaternorthwoods.com/directory/new-odanah/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Manoomin Celebration Powwow takes place every August in New Odanah to mark the wild rice harvest rhythm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greaternorthwoods.com/directory/new-odanah/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Local residents generally consider New Odanah to be part of Odanah, the only name appearing on state and county maps.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Odanah%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Bad River Band tribal government operates the Bad River Lodge and Casino as well as other enterprises in New Odanah.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
